From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: add software dimming

The GAMESCOPE_SOFTWARE_DIMMING atom carries a backlight floor, clamped to
the backlight maximum. Requests at or above it pass through untouched;
below it the panel is held at the floor and the remainder is rendered as a
digital dim factor, luminance-matched to the panel's response so the
slider keeps its perceived scale. AMOLED DDICs track worst at low drive,
crushing shadows and desaturating; holding the panel at the floor
preserves channel ratios and near-black separation at a code-range cost
the output dither covers.

The factor applies to Gamma 2.2 encoded outputs, on the PQ path after
tone mapping so highlights dim uniformly, and Vulkan composition is
forced while it is active so direct scanout cannot bypass it. Write
failures leave the mode inert or hold the previous pin while the panel
provably still shows it; the saved request is restored once it no longer
falls below the floor or the floor is cleared.

The backlight device defaults to the first entry in /sys/class/backlight
and can be selected with GAMESCOPE_SOFTWARE_DIMMING_BACKLIGHT.

